# Build context exclusions for the backend image.
#
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS
# ----------------------------------------
# Two of these lines are security controls rather than build hygiene:
#
#   .env        The real environment file holds DATABASE_URL with the database password,
#               SECRET_KEY and JWT_SECRET. Without this exclusion `COPY . /app/backend`
#               bakes all of them into a layer, where they remain readable by anyone who
#               can pull the image - and `docker history` will not show them because they
#               arrive through a COPY rather than a RUN.
#
#   .venv/      A 500 MB virtual environment built for the host. Copying it in would
#               roughly triple the image and shadow the one built in the builder stage.
#
# `.dockerignore` is also the difference between a 30-second build and a five-minute one.

# -- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.pgpass
credentials.json

# -- local state that must never ship -------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
pytest-of-*/

# -- test and development artefacts ----------------------------------------
tests/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
test.db

# -- version control and tooling -------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml

# -- documentation ---------------------------------------------------------
README*
CHANGELOG*
docs/
*.md

# -- editors ---------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
